  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="DA">Strengthening and Advocating Freedom of Religion or Belief in South Asia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="DA">SAFFoRB, as a civil society organizations Forum with members comprising human rights organisations, NGO&#x2019;s, religious and belief actors from Bangladesh, India, Myanmar, Nepal, Pakistan, and Sri Lanka, is committed to working for a just world where freedom of religion or belief is respected, protected and promoted. It continues to build solidarity and partnership and mobilizes a diverse set of stakeholders to advocate for freedom of religion or belief (FoRB) as enshrined in the Universal Declaration of Human Rights (UDHR) and the International Convention on Civil and Political Rights (IPCCR) across the countries.  SAFFoRB recognises the need for civil society organisations to be more active and visible, engage with women and youth, promote inclusiveness and pluralism, and strive to instil values of respect, dignity, freedom of expression,FoRB and minority rights.  Therefore, this project will focus on building capacities of civil society organisations in training, networking, advocacy on FoRB and State accountability.  The working principles will be based on the fundamental rights enshrined in the country&#x2019;s constitution and UDHR/ICCPR.</narrative>
  </description>
